  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(r_1\\) and \\(r_2\\) are the distinct real roots of \\(x^2+px+8=0,\\) then it must follow that:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\lvert r_1+r_2\\rvert\\gt4\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\lvert r_1\\rvert\\gt3\\) or \\(\\lvert r_2\\rvert\\gt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\lvert r_1\\rvert\\gt2\\) and \\(\\lvert r_2\\rvert\\gt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(r_1\\lt0\\) and \\(r_2\\lt0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\lvert r_1+r_2\\rvert\\lt4\\sqrt2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The discriminant condition is \\(p^2-32\\gt0,\\) so \\(\\lvert p\\rvert\\gt4\\sqrt2.\\) By Vieta’s formulas, \\(r_1+r_2=-p,\\) and therefore \\[ \\lvert r_1+r_2\\rvert=\\lvert p\\rvert\\gt4\\sqrt2. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Distinct real roots require the discriminant to be positive",
        "Use \\(r_1+r_2=-p\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
